// The deploy target (issue #25): Deploy-to-Cloudflare buttons and Workers Builds read the
// Wrangler config from the repository root, and the default deploy command `npx wrangler
// deploy` runs there — so the steward Worker's config lives here, pointing into the monorepo
// (ADR-0001 decision 2) instead of apps/steward/. Local dev/tests pass
// `--config ../../wrangler.jsonc` from apps/steward.
//
// SERVER_KEY, SETUP_TOKEN, and MODEL_KEY are secrets, deliberately NOT declared here: they
// are generated at deploy time through the Deploy-to-Cloudflare form (root .dev.vars.example
// + cloudflare.bindings descriptions in the root package.json) or set manually with
// `wrangler secret put`. See docs/deploy.md.
//
// The steward's model selection (issue #6, ADR-0001 decision 11) is deploy config — set
// `vars.STEWARD_MODEL` here to override the default deepseek/deepseek-flash (the eval
// baseline), e.g.:
//   "vars": { "STEWARD_MODEL": "{\"provider\": \"deepseek\", \"modelId\": \"deepseek-v4-pro\"}" }
// The daily budget soft cap (issue #28, ADR-0001 decision 15) is deploy config too: set
// `vars.DAILY_BUDGET_USD` (dollars per UTC day) to override the default $1 — past it,
// event/routine/follow-up wakes stop reaching the model while done reports, fallback
// pushes, digests, and replies to the owner continue:
//   "vars": { "DAILY_BUDGET_USD": "0.5" }
// The API key never rides in vars: it is the sealed sh_model row (seeded from MODEL_KEY at
// deploy, or set via setModelConfig), and the provider is built with an inline
// auth.apiKey.resolve (spike bug 7). A missing key or unknown provider/model fails visibly
// (`sh_run` settles `unanswered`), never with a silently different model.
{
  "name": "shepherd-steward",
  "main": "apps/steward/src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-10",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [{ "name": "Steward", "class_name": "Steward" }]
  },
  "migrations": [{ "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["Steward"] }]
}
